\section{Grouped and direct arguments}{

Settings documented by an option constructor may also be supplied directly.
For example, \code{concept_name = "heart_rate"} and
\code{concepts = concept_options(concept_name = "heart_rate")} specify the same
setting. Supplying both forms raises an error. Unknown argument names are
rejected. Layer selection is also accepted directly, for example
\code{run_one_source("mimic_iii", stages = "run_concepts", layers = "flat")}.

Name arguments after \code{src_name}, \code{db_name}, and \code{base_dir} when updating a
positional call. Option-group names must be exact; \code{cohort} remains a cohort
selection setting and is not an abbreviation for \code{cohort_selection}.
